How It Works
Our solution is to create a single, automated release report that brings together all the important information from different tools into one place. Instead of checking multiple reports, everyone gets one clear email with:
	Code quality and security results (from SonarQube, Black Duck, Checkmarx)
	Jira story updates and feature summaries
	Test results
	An AI-generated summary of code changes
The process is fully automated using GitHub Actions. When code is pushed to a release branch, the workflow collects all the data, formats it into an easy-to-read HTML email, and sends it to the team. This saves time, reduces manual work, and makes it easy for everyone to see the full release picture at a glance.


PlantUML diagram
Architecture diagram explanation:
The process starts when a developer pushes code to a release branch in the GitHub repository. This action triggers a GitHub Actions workflow. The workflow automatically gathers data from several tools: SonarQube for code quality, Black Duck and Checkmarx for security, Jira for story updates, and an AI service for code summaries.
The system fetches all Karate test cases linked to each Jira Feature. It then checks which of these test cases were actually executed by comparing them with the BDD report. The final report clearly shows:
Which test cases were validated (executed and passed)
Which test cases failed
Which test cases were not validated (not executed at all)
This gives the Product Owner a clear view of BDD test case coverage and validation status for every Jira Feature in the release.

Finally all the collected results are combined by an HTML Email Generator, which creates a clear, unified release report. Finally, the report is sent to stakeholders by email, giving everyone a complete view of the release quality in one place. This automation saves time, reduces manual work, and lowers the risk of missing important issues.


